<title>ITALY: Enichem pulls out of S.Korea joint venture.</title>
<headline>Enichem pulls out of S.Korea joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Enichem, the chemical arm of Italy's ENI energy giant, said it will transfer its entire stake in the Hong Kong Petrochemical Company (HKPC) polystyrene joint venture to South Korean oil refiner Yukong Ltd in mid-July.</p>
<p>Yukong will acquire 47.5 percent of shares with voting rights and 50 percent of shares without voting rights.</p>
<p>The venture, run jointly by Yukong and Enichem for five years, produces 140,000 tonnes per year of polystyrene with a turnover of some $80 million.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
